  "name": "llm-memory-meter",
  "description": "Zero-dependency program that reads a language model's official config.json and reports its real memory footprint — weights per quantization format and KV cache per context length — side by side with the widely shared one-line formula, which overestimates a 2026 hybrid model by up to 20x. Companion to the article 'Como saber se um modelo de IA roda no seu computador — e por quê'.",
